1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:46,547 --> 00:00:48,799
EPISODE 2

7
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,831
What are you doing up so late?

8
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,416
What time is it now?

9
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:25,919
[Miyoung] What are you still doing
up at this hour? Huh?

10
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:27,504
Something like this.

11
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:31,216
What... What's all this? Huh?

12
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,342
[Youjin] Cool, isn't it?

13
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:35,846
So now you want to be a cartoonist
instead of a designer?

14
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:39,600
No, your daughter
is going to get her PhD now.

15
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,810
-Thank you.
-Goodbye.

16
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:46,815
Huh?

17
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:51,320
Oh, Minjae.
I want the expensive coffee too.

18
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:54,740
I'm sorry, but could I get a refund?

19
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,116
-You'd like a refund?
-Yes.

20
00:01:56,199 --> 00:01:57,534
Please insert your card.

21
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:18,055
[Youjin] I double-majored
in fashion and mathematics.

22
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,432
So I've completed
all the required coursework.

23
00:02:21,058 --> 00:02:22,976
My grades aren't that bad, either.

24
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:27,689
I scored over 500 on the TEPS too.

25
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:32,903
But why do you suddenly want to switch
to a completely different major?

26
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:34,321
Uh...

27
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:36,990
I've always liked tinkering with machines.

28
00:02:37,074 --> 00:02:39,660
I was good at building things
with LEGOs too.

29
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:41,995
I even won an award for it as a kid.

30
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:43,205
LEGOs?

31
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,668
Yeah. And I can code too.

32
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:48,919
Oh?

33
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:54,257
Then do you know how to use
MATLAB or SolidWorks too?

34
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:57,386
No. What are those?

35
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,971
You don't.

36
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:02,432
I don't know what they are...

37
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:05,602
but I can learn.

38
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:10,023
I'm a fast learner.
And once I start something, I go all out.

39
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:16,405
I have never written a mechanical
engineering research proposal before.

40
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:17,823
So if you could take a look...

41
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:18,907
But...

42
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:25,622
if you like machines
and you're good at building with LEGOs,

43
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:27,624
they can be your hobbies.

44
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,251
Why go so far as to switch majors?

45
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,046
Well, that's because I...

46
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:38,093
Fashion and textiles just wasn't for me.

47
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:43,265
It turns out
I don't have any talent for it.

48
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:48,395
"It turns out"?

49
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:52,858
But what about all you've learned?
What a waste.

50
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:56,987
All the time and money
over the past four years will go to waste.

51
00:03:58,405 --> 00:04:00,699
And what if you get into grad school,

52
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:05,370
and it turns out
that you don't have any talent

53
00:04:06,538 --> 00:04:08,123
for mechanical engineering?

54
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:10,375
Are you going to switch to business then?

55
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:22,345
[muttering] Look at you, so smart.
What are you, judge and jury?

56
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:24,139
[Minjae] Pardon?

57
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,100
[Youjin] I mean,

58
00:04:27,601 --> 00:04:31,062
maybe you should've gone to law school
instead of engineering school.

59
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,523
Just a random thought.

60
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,360
What I'm saying is,

61
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:41,448
switching majors isn't something
you should decide on rashly like that.

62
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,075
First, everything you learned is wasted.

63
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,578
Plus, won't you feel guilty
toward your parents?

64
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:52,584
Anyway, you've still got some time,
so take your time and think it over.

65
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,881
Are you angry?

66
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,592
No, I'm not angry.

67
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:01,843
I think you're angry.

68
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:04,554
I don't get angry so easily.

69
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:16,900
What is it?

70
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:19,486
What?

71
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:21,404
It's nothing.

72
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:25,617
[Hangyeol] <i>He was sitting</i>
<i>side by side with a woman,</i>

73
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,662
looking at something on a laptop.

74
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:30,831
Was she pretty? Was she a pretty woman?

75
00:05:30,914 --> 00:05:32,332
[Hangyeol] She was gorgeous.

76
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:34,668
Is she in our program?
One of the younger students?

77
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:38,171
No, she's not in our program.
She's some woman I don't know.

78
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,759
He was looking at something on a laptop
with some pretty woman you don't know?

79
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:44,261
Sitting side by side?

80
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,763
How pretty? As pretty as aespa? IVE?

81
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,057
No, not like that.

82
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,978
You know, that American model.

83
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,437
Which American model?

84
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,399
I can't remember her name all of a sudden.

85
00:05:57,482 --> 00:06:00,151
She's really beautiful
and has a baby face.

86
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:02,070
She's been married three times.

87
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:04,531
She's been married three times?

88
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,700
That's how pretty she is.

89
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:09,452
Beautiful women
get three, four chances at marriage.

90
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:12,122
For women like that,
it's polyandry, not polygyny.

91
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,457
All right, hold on. I'll just ask.

92
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,542
[Hangyeol] Ask who?

93
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:17,586
-Chacha.
-[line ringing]

94
00:06:17,669 --> 00:06:20,797
[hesitating] Hey, Seohyun,
you picked up fast. Are you busy?

95
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:24,259
I just wanted to ask you something. Yeah.

96
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:28,763
So, Hangyeol saw Minjae with some woman.

97
00:06:28,847 --> 00:06:31,766
Uh-huh. No.
She's not a student in our program.

98
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:36,104
Anyway, he says
she's really pretty and baby-faced

99
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:38,565
and looks like an American model, yeah.

100
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,859
Is that Seohyun?
Do you think she would know?

101
00:06:43,862 --> 00:06:46,072
Oh, you saw her too?

102
00:06:46,156 --> 00:06:47,657
She saw her? She says she did?

103
00:06:47,741 --> 00:06:50,035
See? I said I saw her.
I really saw her. Seriously...

104
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:54,331
[Taeho] Seohyun. So who is she?
Yeah, she's not in our program.

105
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:56,291
-[door opens]
-[whispers] He's here.

106
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,376
Hey.

107
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:06,801
What's with the weird vibe here?

108
00:07:12,724 --> 00:07:15,477
Okay, so this is the load torque
on the knee,

109
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,062
and this is the friction torque.

110
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,647
DANNY WALKING MODEL VALIDATION

111
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:22,275
The little bits of friction
generated in the gears and the belt

112
00:07:22,359 --> 00:07:23,360
are hard to notice,

113
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,445
but they play a bigger role
than you'd think.

114
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:28,573
But we only factored the load torque
into the simulation.

115
00:07:28,657 --> 00:07:31,159
So the robot seemed to walk fine at first.

116
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:34,621
But on the actual robot,
the friction torque acts on it too,

117
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:38,416
so the knee hesitates a little
before it starts moving.

118
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:43,004
It's about time
I sent you to Dieland, isn't it?

119
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:44,089
Focus, will you?

120
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:45,256
I...

121
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:48,551
I honestly thought... [clears throat]

122
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:50,970
...of you as my soulmate,

123
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:52,055
until now.

124
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:57,227
Your soulmate is your girlfriend,
who is in Daejeon now.

125
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,311
[Taeho] Minjae,

126
00:07:58,395 --> 00:08:03,942
I truly thought of you
as my own brother, you know?

127
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:06,277
But... [sighs]

128
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:10,198
...how come I didn't know something
even Chacha knew?

129
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:12,033
That really hurt my feelings.

130
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,118
The thing is...

131
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:15,453
there's nothing.

132
00:08:15,537 --> 00:08:17,247
I have nothing to tell you.

133
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,082
Stop it and just be honest with me.

134
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,625
What do you mean, be honest?

135
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,461
-[Taeho sighs]
-Are you dating that woman?

136
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:25,797
No, there's nothing going on between us.

137
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:29,509
I saw the two of you sitting side by side,
watching a movie and giggling.

138
00:08:30,093 --> 00:08:32,721
I wasn't giggling,
I wasn't watching a movie,

139
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,139
and there's nothing going on.

140
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:36,891
-I've said it three times now.
-[Taeho] Then prove it.

141
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:38,476
Prove what, and how?

142
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:42,397
If there's really nothing between you two
and you're being honest, then...

143
00:08:43,148 --> 00:08:44,441
set Hangyeol up with her.

144
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,110
-What?
-Yeah.

145
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,612
Set me up with her.

146
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:51,656
[Taeho] He's really into her.

147
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:53,908
Yeah, she's so beautiful.

148
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:57,203
I like her. Set me up with her.

149
00:08:57,287 --> 00:09:00,707
Dude, respect the pecking order.
He has to set me up first.

150
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:04,210
You didn't even get a look at her.
Why would you be set up with her?

151
00:09:04,294 --> 00:09:05,712
[Minjae tapping on board] That's enough.

152
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,881
Stop talking nonsense. Where were we?

153
00:09:08,423 --> 00:09:13,094
Right, anyway, now we need to incorporate
this friction model into the simulation.

154
00:09:13,178 --> 00:09:14,179
[Hangyeol] If...

155
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:20,226
If you don't set me up on a date,
I'm going to quit the lab.

156
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:21,728
What?

157
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:27,233
I'll also quit the lab
if you don't set me up on a date.

158
00:09:29,319 --> 00:09:30,695
Well done, guys.

159
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:33,865
[sighs] Fine, quit then.
Just quit. Go on and quit.

160
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:34,991
Quit the lab.

161
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:38,745
I'll talk to the professor,
so you two bring me your withdrawal forms.

162
00:09:38,828 --> 00:09:42,791
[chuckles] Right, Chansoo,
you got an offer from KAIST, right?

163
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:43,875
-Yes.
-Yeah.

164
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:46,252
Professor Hwang Semin's lab
reached out to me.

165
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:48,671
They asked if I'd join them
for the upcoming WRS.

166
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:53,885
KAIST is preparing for the WRS?
But they didn't participate last year.

167
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,595
Not sure, but they are this year.

168
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,679
Is that so?

169
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,932
[Hangyeol] What's the WRS?

170
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,684
-[groans]
-[in English] World Robot Summit.

171
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,398
[in Korean] Are you setting me up
on a date or not?

172
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,748
See? She's not answering.

173
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:25,500
-She will.
-[line connects]

174
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:26,668
[Youjin on phone] <i>Hello?</i>

175
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,169
Hello?

176
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:32,173
Ah, I wasn't doing anything.

177
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,969
There's a book I need to read,
so I was reading that.

178
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:39,931
Oh. It's nothing serious.
I just wanted to ask you something.

179
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:43,685
Sure, go ahead and ask.

180
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:49,107
Boyfriend?

181
00:10:51,109 --> 00:10:54,279
But why do you want to know that?

182
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:58,950
[chuckles] Why do you care
if I have a boyfriend or not...

183
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,079
No. I don't have a boyfriend.

184
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,499
-Why do you ask?
-[digital door lock beeping]

185
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,588
Hey, why are you home today?

186
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:17,135
[Youjin] I can't really talk right now.
Can we talk later? Yes.

187
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,013
-[grunts]
-Yes.

188
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:24,934
Mom. Lim Youjin is seeing someone.

189
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,736
You're seeing someone
these days, aren't you?

190
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:36,988
No, I'm not.

191
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:39,324
Then why did you hide earlier?

192
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:43,411
What do you mean, hide?
I just wanted to talk somewhere quiet.

193
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,664
[Miyoung] Are you really
not seeing anyone?

194
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:50,627
No. I'm way too busy studying, you know.

195
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,838
I barely get any sleep as it is.
How would I even have time to date?

196
00:11:53,922 --> 00:11:58,134
Exactly. You're in the prime of your life,
and all you do is sit at that desk.

197
00:11:58,718 --> 00:12:00,345
Aren't you going to get married?

198
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,014
I'm never getting married.

199
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,891
I'm going to live with you forever.

200
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:08,019
You can't do that.
You have to get married, still.

201
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:10,813
Dad, do you believe that?

202
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:13,566
The three biggest lies in Korea

203
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,777
are old folks saying,
"I should just die already,"

204
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:19,447
and daughters saying, "I'm going to live
with Mom and Dad forever."

205
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:22,617
What was the last one?
There are three of them.

206
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,786
They're not lies.
They're just trying to be nice.

207
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:28,498
See? This is why daughters
are different from sons.

208
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:31,376
This is why it's nice to have a daughter.

209
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,710
-Mmm-hmm.
-[Miyoung] Yeah.

210
00:12:32,794 --> 00:12:36,923
What? What's wrong with sons?
Why are you playing favorites?

211
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:38,675
When did I play favorites?

212
00:12:38,758 --> 00:12:40,260
Just now.

213
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,096
Lim Youjin is always right, isn't she?

214
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:47,684
Even if she told you
<i>doenjang</i> was made from red beans,

215
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,018
you'd believe her, right?

216
00:12:49,102 --> 00:12:50,103
Yes.

217
00:12:50,812 --> 00:12:53,940
It's <i>meju,</i> not <i>doenjang.</i>
It's <i>"Meju</i> is made from red beans."

218
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:56,901
It's <i>meju?</i> Hmm.

219
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,198
So you're not seeing anyone?

220
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:03,992
Mmm.

221
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,451
I don't have time for it.

222
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:09,038
I mean, it's okay if you date. It's okay.

223
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:11,749
Just let me meet the guy first.

224
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:14,043
Okay.

225
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,130
I don't ask for much.

226
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,424
Just someone who's hardworking,

227
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:25,179
respects his elders, and is healthy,
with all four limbs intact.

228
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:28,099
Other than that, I don't ask for anything.

229
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:31,311
[Miyoung] What do you mean,
all four limbs?

230
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:33,104
Who doesn't have four limbs?

231
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,897
-[chuckles]
-[Yongseok] Some people don't.

232
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,232
You know, people with disabilities.

233
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,401
-[Miyoung] You little...
-Come on.

234
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:39,944
[Miyoung] No more food for you.

235
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:07,573
If you keep pulling all-nighters,
your skin's going to become dull.

236
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:12,245
I know. It'll get all dry, right?

237
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:14,372
What am I going to do?

238
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:17,917
Are you really not seeing anyone?

239
00:15:19,127 --> 00:15:22,046
No. Lim Youseong got it totally wrong.

240
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:23,131
Hmm.

241
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:26,968
I'm actually more worried
about your love life

242
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:29,053
than your grad school entrance exam.

243
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,683
Do you want me to set you up with someone?

244
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:38,896
One of our customers at the auto shop
owns a huge building near Gangnam Station.

245
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,275
I said
you go to Seohan National University,

246
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,318
and they asked to see a picture of you.

247
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:47,530
So I showed them one, and they said,

248
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:50,700
"She's this pretty, and she's smart too?"

249
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,369
They'd love you as a daughter-in-law.

250
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:57,331
Guess their son
didn't do too well in school.

251
00:15:57,415 --> 00:16:02,044
I didn't ask.
Well, I don't even need to ask.

252
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:05,173
Any school that's not Harvard
is below Seohan anyway.

253
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,511
Yeah, never mind. [clears throat]

254
00:16:11,179 --> 00:16:12,263
He's no good.

255
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:16,601
You need a man who's smart.
A dumb guy won't do.

256
00:16:18,436 --> 00:16:19,812
[Youjin] Yeah.

257
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:23,733
He has to be handsome and tall.

258
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,235
[Youjin] Yeah.

259
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:28,362
A woman

260
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:32,450
should always be with a man who loves her

261
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:35,328
more than she loves him.

262
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,914
He's smart, handsome, and tall.

263
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:41,209
What if he doesn't like me?
That could happen.

264
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:44,629
That's just not possible.

265
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:47,882
I'm not saying this
because you're my daughter.

266
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:50,885
You're really cool and attractive.

267
00:16:52,053 --> 00:16:56,474
But I'm not some goddess, like Venus.
I may not be everyone's type.

268
00:16:58,935 --> 00:17:00,937
Type isn't the issue with you.

269
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:04,148
Any guy who doesn't like you is an idiot.

270
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:08,736
Don't date someone like that.

271
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:14,992
But what if I like the idiot anyway?

272
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:18,162
You can't always control
how you feel, right?

273
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:22,208
Hmm?

274
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:41,852
No.

275
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:49,860
Hmm.

276
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:02,456
At least get the dirt
and sand off for now.

277
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:04,709
I'm okay.

278
00:18:04,792 --> 00:18:06,127
No, hurry and wipe it off.

279
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:10,214
If not cleaned right away,
it could lead to ulcers and infection.

280
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:50,504
Hey.

281
00:18:51,797 --> 00:18:52,798
You're here.

282
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,346
What the... You guys came together?

283
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:02,475
-Come on. Have a seat.
-Hmm?

284
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:07,104
[Minjae] Hmm.

285
00:19:07,188 --> 00:19:10,107
So, this is Lim Youjin.

286
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:15,696
And this is Chansoo.
We work in the same lab. Bae Chansoo.

287
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,491
-Hello.
-Hello.

288
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:21,452
I've heard so much about you.
You're really beautiful.

289
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,624
-Here's the menu.
-[Minjae] Thank you.

290
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:28,084
Why don't we order first?

291
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:31,337
Everything's good here.

292
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,215
The creamy shrimp pasta is great,
and so is the risotto.

293
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,511
There are more in the back.

294
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:41,222
Here. Soup. Appetizers.

295
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:43,474
Order everything you want.

296
00:19:44,392 --> 00:19:47,436
Yes. Go ahead and order
everything you want. It's on me.

297
00:19:48,813 --> 00:19:49,814
Okay.

298
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:54,026
Then I'll just get
the creamy shrimp pasta.

299
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:56,237
The creamy shrimp pasta. And you, Chansoo?

300
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,447
Then I'll get the creamy shrimp pasta too.

301
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:00,700
Two creamy shrimp pastas.

302
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:03,786
-Excuse me, we'd like to order.
-[server] Yes.

303
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:07,039
Could we have two orders
of creamy shrimp pasta, please?

304
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:09,208
-All right. Thank you.
-Yes, thank you.

305
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:19,844
Right.

306
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:23,764
I've got some more work to do
back at the lab, so I'll get going.

307
00:20:23,848 --> 00:20:25,975
Enjoy your meal,
and get to know each other.

308
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,810
Your matchmaker will leave you to it.

309
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:41,699
-Hmm.
-[bell tinkles]

310
00:20:55,171 --> 00:20:58,215
Actually, I haven't been
on many blind dates,

311
00:20:58,299 --> 00:20:59,884
so this feels a little awkward.

312
00:21:00,718 --> 00:21:01,719
[Youjin] Hmm.

313
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:05,556
I didn't know this was a blind date.

314
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:13,481
You didn't know about this?
You didn't know?

315
00:21:14,482 --> 00:21:19,320
No, I did hear it's a blind date.
I did hear about it, but...

316
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:24,742
Sometimes, I get the wrong idea
in my head, and I get tunnel vision.

317
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,536
I can be a real idiot sometimes.

318
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:32,958
I see.

319
00:21:33,501 --> 00:21:34,752
-Yeah.
-[bell tinkles]

320
00:21:44,512 --> 00:21:46,263
Excuse me, are you Mr. Bae Chansoo?

321
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:49,600
Oh, you are. I was right.

322
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:53,896
I was just walking by
and thought it was you.

323
00:21:56,148 --> 00:22:00,069
Hello. I work with Chansoo in the lab.

324
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:01,737
I'm Choi Hangyeol.

325
00:22:01,821 --> 00:22:02,822
[Youjin] Oh...

326
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:08,452
I'm not interrupting anything, am I?

327
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:10,412
[Youjin] No, not at all.

328
00:22:11,497 --> 00:22:14,291
I mean, what a coincidence,
running into him here.

329
00:22:14,375 --> 00:22:17,711
I'm just so happy to see him.
What should I do now?

330
00:22:18,379 --> 00:22:22,258
Do you mind if I join you for a bit?
Just for a moment.

331
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,677
-Sure, it's okay. Please have a seat here.
-Oh.

332
00:22:32,935 --> 00:22:34,937
[whispering] Dude,
what are you doing here?

333
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,522
[whispering] It's okay.

334
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:41,068
I haven't eaten yet, actually.

335
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,361
Can I order something too?

336
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:45,364
Yes, of course.
If you haven't eaten yet...

337
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:47,658
-Excuse me.
-[server] Yes.

338
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:48,909
[Youjin] We'd like to order.

339
00:22:48,993 --> 00:22:50,786
[whispering] What on earth
are you doing here?

340
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:55,791
[softly] I saw her first.
I deserve a chance too.

341
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:58,252
-Water?
-[Hangyeol] Oh.

342
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:11,181
Is that Chansoo and Hangyeol,
by any chance?

343
00:23:11,682 --> 00:23:14,560
Ah, it is. [laughs awkwardly]

344
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:18,230
Hello. What a coincidence.

345
00:23:21,442 --> 00:23:23,110
Funny running into you like this.

346
00:23:27,323 --> 00:23:28,699
Hello.

347
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:33,412
I'm lab mates with them.

348
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:35,080
-[Youjin] Hmm.
-[chuckling]

349
00:23:35,706 --> 00:23:38,709
-[Hangyeol chuckles awkwardly]
-Man. How funny is this? [laughing]

350
00:23:40,711 --> 00:23:43,714
-[Hangyeol] So, would you like some pasta?
-Yeah, I'd love that.

351
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,097
-Yes, come in.
-[door opens]

352
00:23:55,935 --> 00:23:58,312
Is this Professor Ahn Jaehong's lab?

353
00:23:58,395 --> 00:24:00,940
Yes, this is Professor Ahn's lab.
And who are you?

354
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:06,320
Uh...

355
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:10,407
Hello. I'm Kim Sejin.
I study electronic engineering at KAIST.

356
00:24:10,491 --> 00:24:14,370
KAIST electronic... Right.
I got your email. Come on in.

357
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:15,454
Man.

358
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:17,122
So everyone misunderstood.

359
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,207
Yeah.

360
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:22,294
But really, there's absolutely nothing
going on between us.

361
00:24:22,378 --> 00:24:25,965
Mr. Park Minjae and I
just know each other's names and faces.

362
00:24:26,048 --> 00:24:27,049
[Taeho] Hmm.

363
00:24:27,841 --> 00:24:32,096
Park Minjae isn't exactly my type, either.
I can't stand guys like him.

364
00:24:34,223 --> 00:24:36,850
I was just asking him for some advice

365
00:24:36,934 --> 00:24:39,812
about applying to grad school that day.

366
00:24:41,689 --> 00:24:44,191
Grad school? Our program?

367
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:48,529
I double-majored in fashion and textiles
and mathematics.

368
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:51,490
I've taken the required courses,
and my grades aren't bad.

369
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:52,825
And I scored over 500 on TEPS.

370
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:58,080
Have you always been interested
in mechanical engineering?

371
00:24:58,163 --> 00:25:00,582
Yes, I've always liked
tinkering with machines.

372
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:04,211
I won first prize
in a LEGO-building contest once.

373
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:06,088
I can code too.

374
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:11,510
[Hangyeol] Anything involving robots?

375
00:25:12,803 --> 00:25:15,389
We're a robotics lab.

376
00:25:17,141 --> 00:25:20,394
Our professor is really great.

377
00:25:20,477 --> 00:25:21,478
[Hangyeol] Yeah.

378
00:25:21,562 --> 00:25:24,690
There are also scholarships available,
and the stipend's pretty good too.

379
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:25,899
It's honestly a great lab.

380
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:30,946
Have you reached out to any other labs?

381
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,614
No, not yet.

382
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:35,325
I don't even know if I can get in or not.

383
00:25:35,409 --> 00:25:38,871
But with grades like yours,
of course you'd get in.

384
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:41,540
Do you know how hard it is
to find lab slaves these days?

385
00:25:43,751 --> 00:25:48,714
Actually, I'm basically the one

386
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:52,384
who chooses the students for our lab.

387
00:25:53,594 --> 00:25:56,221
You should see the Robot Control Room
while you're here.

388
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:57,639
It's right around the corner.

389
00:25:57,723 --> 00:25:58,724
Okay.

390
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:04,104
Right, I heard
you've completed the URP at KAIST.

391
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:05,522
[Sejin] Yes.

392
00:26:05,606 --> 00:26:09,276
[Minjae] May I ask why you reached out
to us instead of their lab?

393
00:26:10,611 --> 00:26:14,031
[Sejin] I read Professor Ahn's works.
His research seems like a good fit.

394
00:26:14,531 --> 00:26:17,659
I also heard
his lab is basically a free-range lab.

395
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:20,746
Our reputation made it to your school?

396
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:21,997
-[Sejin] Yeah.
-[Minjae exclaims]

397
00:26:22,498 --> 00:26:23,499
[Minjae] After you.

398
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:27,086
-[groans softly]
-Yes.

399
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:31,799
Well, uh, our lab is pretty hands-off.

400
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:36,428
Professor Ahn values student autonomy
over short-term results,

401
00:26:36,512 --> 00:26:39,056
which is how we got
the whole free-range reputation...

402
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:41,016
I didn't mean that in a bad way.

403
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:44,394
I like having autonomy in my research,
so that's actually a plus for me.

404
00:26:44,478 --> 00:26:46,230
Really? That's good to hear.

405
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,067
-Your leg...
-Yes?

406
00:26:50,150 --> 00:26:51,360
Is your leg okay?

407
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:53,821
No, I'm fine. It's just...

408
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:58,242
I have a prosthetic right leg,

409
00:26:58,325 --> 00:27:00,536
so it can be
a little inconvenient sometimes.

410
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:04,998
Yeah, I heard you had your leg amputated
because of cancer.

411
00:27:08,919 --> 00:27:12,464
Even that got around?
All the way to Daejeon?

412
00:27:12,548 --> 00:27:16,093
Well, I wouldn't say it got around.
You're just that famous.

413
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:20,055
Famous for what?
For being a disabled researcher?

414
00:27:20,556 --> 00:27:22,391
Well, that could be part of it.

415
00:27:24,393 --> 00:27:27,855
Ah, I heard you were a competitive swimmer
in high school too.

416
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:30,399
Yeah, I guess.

417
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:32,651
You don't swim anymore?

418
00:27:35,821 --> 00:27:37,030
No, I don't.

419
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:39,074
Why not?

420
00:27:40,742 --> 00:27:43,954
What do you mean, why not?
Because I don't want to, obviously.

421
00:27:45,122 --> 00:27:48,584
[Sejin] Well, it's still early spring,
so the water will probably be cold.

422
00:27:51,712 --> 00:27:53,922
Are you always this insensitive?

423
00:27:57,426 --> 00:27:59,636
Well, no one's ever called me that before.

424
00:28:02,598 --> 00:28:03,599
Ah.

425
00:28:04,474 --> 00:28:06,810
Some people do call me nuts, though.

426
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:13,108
This is a prototype robot
that's been passed down to us.

427
00:28:13,191 --> 00:28:15,235
-You said you were into LEGOs, right?
-[Youjin] Yes.

428
00:28:15,319 --> 00:28:17,613
Right. Just like the joints
on a LEGO model move,

429
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,657
these motors
let the robot move all its joints.

430
00:28:20,741 --> 00:28:21,742
These motors here.

431
00:28:22,618 --> 00:28:25,370
The motors... Come this way.

432
00:28:25,454 --> 00:28:28,165
-This... Look here.

433
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:31,585
[Hangyeol] Youjin, you haven't seen
something like this before, have you?

434
00:28:31,668 --> 00:28:33,462
-[Youjin] What?
-[Hangyeol] Something like this.

435
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:34,546
What's this?

436
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:36,548
This is what we call a robot hand.

437
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:40,802
It can sense touch and has joints too,
just like a human hand.

438
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:43,305
Want to say hi? A handshake?

439
00:28:44,222 --> 00:28:45,974
-[Youjin chuckles]
-[Taeho in robotic voice] Youjin.

440
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:47,809
Youjin.

441
00:28:49,019 --> 00:28:50,395
Nice to meet you.

442
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:54,316
-[in normal voice] Cool, isn't it?
-Yeah.

443
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:57,736
Youjin, this is the robot
we're making these days.

444
00:28:57,819 --> 00:29:01,448
You can come closer and touch it
if you want. It's okay.

445
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:04,868
Its name is Danny.

446
00:29:05,869 --> 00:29:07,079
As in Daniel Craig.

447
00:29:07,788 --> 00:29:10,207
The James Bond actor. You know him, right?

448
00:29:11,458 --> 00:29:12,459
Oh.

449
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:14,211
Cool, right?

450
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:19,424
So Danny is a male robot?

451
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:22,511
Yeah, he's male.

452
00:29:23,637 --> 00:29:25,263
So, is there a female robot too?

453
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,057
Hmm? Uh...

454
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:31,937
Well, I wouldn't say it's male.

455
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:34,773
It's more like... unisex.

456
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:41,238
It can be a man and a woman.

457
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,282
[Hangyeol] Oh, like this.

458
00:29:45,534 --> 00:29:46,702
-Youjin.
-Yes.

459
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:49,663
Hold this bat here. Now, watch me.

460
00:29:50,247 --> 00:29:54,251
Stand here
and pull it back as far as you can.

461
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:57,754
Bam! See that? This is how you do it.

462
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:01,341
Yeah. Just stand here and bam!

463
00:30:01,925 --> 00:30:03,385
Hit it nice and loud.

464
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:06,221
-Like this?
-Here, stand in front of it like this.

465
00:30:07,097 --> 00:30:09,391
Like this. And this here...

466
00:30:10,559 --> 00:30:12,269
-Pull it in like this.
-[Youjin] Like this?

467
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:14,396
All right. Then, bam!

468
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:16,898
-It's just a test.
-It's a test. Give it a go.

469
00:30:19,359 --> 00:30:21,028
Huh? [laughs]

470
00:30:21,111 --> 00:30:24,364
No. You can hit it much harder.

471
00:30:26,241 --> 00:30:28,577
Uh, but I feel bad for the robot.

472
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:29,661
I mean...

473
00:30:29,745 --> 00:30:32,205
No, you don't need to feel bad, Youjin.

474
00:30:32,289 --> 00:30:35,042
Imagine it's someone you hate.

475
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:38,336
Think of it as someone you really hate.

476
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:41,089
-Bam! Hit it as hard as you can.
-[Hangyeol] Yeah.

477
00:30:41,173 --> 00:30:43,759
[Chansoo] You don't need
to feel bad for it. It's just a test.

478
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,010
[Hangyeol] It's a test.

479
00:30:45,093 --> 00:30:47,971
[Taeho] An important test to see
how much impact the robot can withstand.

480
00:30:48,055 --> 00:30:49,389
-So just...
-Bam!

481
00:30:49,473 --> 00:30:51,475
-[Taeho] This is a serious test.
-[Chansoo] It's a test.

482
00:30:51,558 --> 00:30:52,559
[Minjae] <i>But...</i>

483
00:30:52,642 --> 00:30:54,269
[Hangyeol] Please take it seriously.

484
00:30:54,352 --> 00:30:58,690
...if you like machines
and you're good at building with LEGOs,

485
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:01,026
they can be your hobbies.

486
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:02,819
Why go so far as to switch majors?

487
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:05,280
<i>What if you get into grad school,</i>

488
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:08,033
<i>and it turns out</i>
<i>that you don't have any talent</i>

489
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:10,619
for mechanical engineering?

490
00:31:11,453 --> 00:31:13,538
Are you going to switch to business then?

491
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:19,211
<i>I've got some more work to do</i>
<i>at the lab, so I'll get going.</i>

492
00:31:19,294 --> 00:31:21,254
<i>Enjoy your meal,</i>
<i>and get to know each other.</i>

493
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:22,964
Your matchmaker will leave you to it.

494
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:30,764
-[Miran] <i>Are you lecturing me right now?</i>
-[others chattering indistinctly]

495
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:34,851
You're obviously so smart.

496
00:31:34,935 --> 00:31:39,606
Who am I to try to guide
or teach someone like you?

497
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:43,193
Just go for it!

498
00:31:44,277 --> 00:31:45,487
Bam!

499
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:53,870
What was that sound?

500
00:31:57,999 --> 00:31:59,918
[groans softly] It's...

501
00:32:00,836 --> 00:32:02,587
[yelling] What are you doing?

502
00:32:05,549 --> 00:32:06,800
[Chansoo] It's not...

503
00:32:11,805 --> 00:32:12,806
[Taeho] We were...

504
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:19,354
Looks like we'll have to end
the tour here today. You can go.

505
00:32:19,437 --> 00:32:20,438
Okay.

506
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:27,571
-You should leave.
-[Taeho] Minjae.

507
00:32:27,654 --> 00:32:29,197
-[Minjae] Don't touch that.
-[Taeho] It was a test.

508
00:32:29,281 --> 00:32:30,532
[Hangyeol] Yeah.

509
00:32:32,909 --> 00:32:34,578
[Taeho softly] Come on, let's go.

510
00:32:35,453 --> 00:32:36,663
Sorry.

511
00:33:04,274 --> 00:33:06,943
-[clicks]
-[motor whirring]

512
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:15,327
-[grunts softly]
-[motor whirring]

513
00:33:38,099 --> 00:33:39,684
-[thuds]
-[groans]

514
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:57,202
I can't take this shit anymore! Damn it!

515
00:34:01,748 --> 00:34:03,500
-[yelling]
-[objects clattering]

516
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:06,855
-[soft whirring]
-[latch clicks]

517
00:35:56,738 --> 00:36:00,450
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

518
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:03,161
[nurse] Mr. Park Minjae.

519
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,245
Yes.

520
00:36:15,632 --> 00:36:17,258
-[groans] Doctor.
-Yeah.

521
00:36:17,342 --> 00:36:19,219
[Minjae] At first,
it was only the skin that hurt,

522
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:21,513
so I thought
it would go away in a few days.

523
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:25,433
But now it hurts so much
I can't even put my prosthetic on.

524
00:36:25,934 --> 00:36:27,686
-You've developed an ulcer.
-What?

525
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:36,653
But it hasn't even been five months
since my last checkup.

526
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:38,405
How did this happen all of a sudden?

527
00:36:38,488 --> 00:36:41,366
You've been busy with work, haven't you?
And lots of stress?

528
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:43,076
-What?
-[doctor] Hardly exercising

529
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:46,538
and eating pizza and fried chicken
for dinner every night, right?

530
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:49,666
You've gained 3.8 kg.

531
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:54,087
Jeez, look right here.
See? It's pretty obvious.

532
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:59,551
You see, a prosthesis is basically
like a piece of clothing made of metal.

533
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:03,722
But unlike a T-shirt or regular clothes,
it doesn't stretch.

534
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:08,268
So your body has to fit the prosthesis,
not the other way around.

535
00:37:09,185 --> 00:37:10,562
Your prosthesis was too tight,

536
00:37:10,645 --> 00:37:13,106
which restricted the blood flow
and caused the ulcer.

537
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:16,234
So don't worry too much about it, okay?

538
00:37:18,528 --> 00:37:19,529
Man.

539
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:21,239
Uh...

540
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:26,995
Wait, so it's not a recurrence
or anything like that?

541
00:37:27,078 --> 00:37:29,706
That's right.
Just keep an eye on your weight.

542
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:34,461
I know you were really worried.
Are you disappointed?

543
00:37:34,544 --> 00:37:36,755
Doctor, what do you mean, disappointed?

544
00:37:37,881 --> 00:37:39,549
I thought it had come back.

545
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,010
I cried my eyes out and freaked out.

546
00:37:42,844 --> 00:37:44,429
How could I be disappointed?

547
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:46,264
Why would you say it like that?

548
00:37:47,474 --> 00:37:49,476
Come on, that's not what I meant.

549
00:37:50,894 --> 00:37:53,563
What I'm saying is,
an ulcer like this is only superficial.

550
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:57,150
It'll heal quickly,
so you don't need to worry.

551
00:37:58,818 --> 00:38:00,528
How about getting back into swimming?

552
00:38:00,612 --> 00:38:03,114
It's a full-body workout
and helps with weight loss.

553
00:38:03,198 --> 00:38:06,034
As a former competitive swimmer,
you'd know better.

554
00:38:08,745 --> 00:38:11,581
Well, I'm not forcing you to do it.

555
00:38:11,664 --> 00:38:14,667
But it's a doctor's recommendation,
so give it some thought.

556
00:40:26,883 --> 00:40:28,509
[staff] We're closing at 10.

557
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:30,845
All right.

558
00:40:52,325 --> 00:40:54,535
[Minjae scoffs] <i>40 million won?</i>

559
00:40:54,619 --> 00:40:57,956
[Taeho] Yeah. They said
we'll probably need to replace the motor

560
00:40:58,039 --> 00:40:59,540
and order a new wrist link.

561
00:41:01,668 --> 00:41:04,754
All right, fine.
I'll tell the professor myself.

562
00:41:04,837 --> 00:41:09,008
Right. Youjin said
she sent an email to Professor Ahn.

563
00:41:09,092 --> 00:41:10,677
Could you please look into that too?

564
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:11,761
[Minjae] Youjin?

565
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,514
Yeah, Lim Youjin.

566
00:41:14,597 --> 00:41:16,099
Lim Youjin from the other day.

567
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,436
[groans] Just thinking about it
pisses me off.

568
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:23,523
What were you guys doing
while she caused all that trouble?

569
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:25,274
Why did you just let it happen?

570
00:41:25,358 --> 00:41:28,695
Well, we didn't know
it'd turn into such a big problem.

571
00:41:29,445 --> 00:41:31,072
Turns out she's really strong.

572
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:37,578
But she was pretty shaken up herself.

573
00:41:37,662 --> 00:41:41,499
She went white as a sheet
and kept apologizing to us. Gosh.

574
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:43,960
It made me feel so bad.

575
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:47,922
Minjae, if we're being honest,

576
00:41:48,006 --> 00:41:49,966
what happened in the lab that day
was on us.

577
00:41:50,049 --> 00:41:52,719
Youjin didn't do anything wrong.

578
00:41:52,802 --> 00:41:55,346
She happened to be there
at the wrong time.

579
00:41:55,430 --> 00:41:57,557
Right? Come on. Right?

580
00:41:59,434 --> 00:42:02,186
Well, since things
have turned out this way,

581
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:05,148
maybe all this happened for a reason.

582
00:42:05,231 --> 00:42:08,359
It'd be great if we could all
work together here in the lab--

583
00:42:08,443 --> 00:42:09,777
I already filled the spot.

584
00:42:09,861 --> 00:42:11,070
-Already?
-Yeah.

585
00:42:11,863 --> 00:42:12,864
Okay.

586
00:42:12,947 --> 00:42:15,116
He's an electrical engineering major
at KAIST.

587
00:42:15,199 --> 00:42:17,243
His papers and grades are both great.

588
00:42:17,326 --> 00:42:20,163
He even did URP in undergrad,
so I hired him right away.

589
00:42:20,246 --> 00:42:24,542
Hold on, are you talking about Samjin
or Sajin or whatever, that KAIST nutjob?

590
00:42:25,168 --> 00:42:26,335
He's not a nutjob.

591
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:29,839
Minjae, everyone in KAIST
knows he's nuts. Okay?

592
00:42:29,922 --> 00:42:32,425
He contacted our school
because they all know he's nuts.

593
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:34,719
I don't care.
A lot of smart people are nuts.

594
00:42:34,802 --> 00:42:38,556
[scoffs] Really? Then I must be nuts too.

595
00:42:38,639 --> 00:42:39,640
Are you not?

596
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:49,358
Yes?

597
00:42:52,862 --> 00:42:54,572
-Hi.
-[Jaehong] Hey, Minjae. Come in.

598
00:42:57,784 --> 00:43:00,078
Did you go to the hospital?
What did they say?

599
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:02,580
Ah, nothing much.

600
00:43:02,663 --> 00:43:05,750
They said I should exercise, lose weight,
and take better care of myself.

601
00:43:05,833 --> 00:43:06,834
-[Jaehong] Yeah?
-Yeah.

602
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:09,629
From the way you're walking,
you seem to be doing better.

603
00:43:09,712 --> 00:43:11,089
Yeah, I'm doing fine. Yes.

604
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:16,385
I got an email
from an interesting student.

605
00:43:16,469 --> 00:43:19,097
-[Minjae] Yes.
-She's a fashion and textiles graduate,

606
00:43:19,180 --> 00:43:21,516
and she wants to study in our program.

607
00:43:23,392 --> 00:43:25,478
Apparently, math was her second major.

608
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:28,940
Math is the foundation
of algorithm design, after all.

609
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:30,691
-But, Professor, we already...
-[line ringing]

610
00:43:30,775 --> 00:43:32,527
Yeah. Wait, one second. Sorry.

611
00:43:33,069 --> 00:43:35,863
-Hello? Hey, Professor Kang.
-[Miran] <i>Hey, Professor Ahn.</i>

612
00:43:35,947 --> 00:43:38,199
-Are you busy now?
-[Miran] <i>I've got time.</i>

613
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:40,493
-Can you talk for a minute?
-[Miran] <i>Yes, sure.</i>

614
00:43:40,576 --> 00:43:42,286
I just wanted to ask you something.

615
00:43:42,370 --> 00:43:44,705
[Miran] <i>Okay, what is it?</i>
<i>Go ahead and ask me now.</i>

616
00:43:44,789 --> 00:43:46,999
-Really? Now?
-[Miran] <i>Yes.</i>

617
00:43:47,083 --> 00:43:48,084
Hmm.

618
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:49,877
Then...

619
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:52,964
How about we meet up and grab a bite?

620
00:43:53,047 --> 00:43:56,217
[Miran] <i>I'd be honored. Are you buying?</i>

621
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,887
Of course, I should buy. Yeah.

622
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:01,681
[Miran] <i>Then,</i>
<i>let's meet at the Faculty Club.</i>

623
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:04,058
-Okay. That's a good choice. Yeah.
-[Miran] <i>Yeah.</i>

624
00:44:04,142 --> 00:44:06,269
-All right. I'll see you there.
-[Miran] <i>See you there.</i>

625
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:08,104
-Okay, bye.
-[Miran] <i>Bye.</i>

626
00:44:09,897 --> 00:44:11,190
Have you had lunch yet?

627
00:44:11,274 --> 00:44:13,693
Sorry? No, I haven't yet.

628
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:15,653
Come with me.

629
00:44:15,736 --> 00:44:16,988
FACULTY CLUB

630
00:44:18,239 --> 00:44:21,659
There you are.

631
00:44:22,243 --> 00:44:23,661
It's been a while.

632
00:44:24,537 --> 00:44:27,081
This is my lab assistant.

633
00:44:27,165 --> 00:44:28,374
Nice to meet you.

634
00:44:28,457 --> 00:44:29,709
I'm Park Minjae.

635
00:44:29,792 --> 00:44:30,793
Mm-hmm.

636
00:44:33,504 --> 00:44:35,715
Gosh, it's been ages.

637
00:44:35,798 --> 00:44:38,342
You only ever call
when you need something.

638
00:44:38,426 --> 00:44:41,721
Yeah. I'm sorry. I've been too busy.

639
00:44:41,804 --> 00:44:43,890
Are you the only busy one here?
What about me?

640
00:44:43,973 --> 00:44:46,893
I know. That's why
I'm treating you to lunch today.

641
00:44:47,393 --> 00:44:49,896
-Excuse me.
-Hello. Can we have the menu, please?

642
00:44:51,981 --> 00:44:52,982
Thank you.

643
00:45:07,622 --> 00:45:08,623
Thank you.

644
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:29,852
[Miran] <i>Lim Youjin?</i>

645
00:45:29,936 --> 00:45:31,270
-Yeah.
-[Miran] Yeah, I know her.

646
00:45:31,354 --> 00:45:32,855
She's one of our graduates.

647
00:45:33,606 --> 00:45:36,776
But I had no idea she'd contacted
the mechanical engineering department.

648
00:45:36,859 --> 00:45:41,697
Yeah, I was surprised too.
She has a pretty unique background.

649
00:45:41,781 --> 00:45:43,783
It's not just her background
that's unique.

650
00:45:43,866 --> 00:45:46,410
She's pretty unique herself.

651
00:45:46,494 --> 00:45:49,330
Yeah? She's unique? Unique how?

652
00:45:50,373 --> 00:45:52,792
Well, how should I put it?

653
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:55,670
She's a bright kid. She's smart.

654
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:59,382
Yeah, looks like she did well
in undergrad. Her grades are good.

655
00:45:59,465 --> 00:46:01,467
But when I say she's smart...

656
00:46:03,052 --> 00:46:05,596
You know, kids these days
aren't like we were at their age.

657
00:46:05,680 --> 00:46:06,681
Ah.

658
00:46:07,556 --> 00:46:10,309
She's book-smart,

659
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:13,020
but she's kind of self-centered?

660
00:46:13,729 --> 00:46:15,439
[Miran] We're educators ourselves,

661
00:46:15,523 --> 00:46:18,359
but something's seriously wrong
with the education system.

662
00:46:18,442 --> 00:46:20,486
Look how hard we push kids to compete.

663
00:46:20,569 --> 00:46:23,948
No one's a friend. Everyone's the enemy.
Everything's about competition.

664
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:25,533
"I have to beat everyone."

665
00:46:25,616 --> 00:46:27,410
"If I don't crush you,
I'm the one who goes down."

666
00:46:27,493 --> 00:46:28,494
That's the mentality.

667
00:46:28,577 --> 00:46:33,457
Yeah, but that's because we adults
failed to teach them better.

668
00:46:33,541 --> 00:46:36,377
At the end of the day,
they're all victims too. Victims.

669
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:39,463
Yeah, exactly. They're all victims.

670
00:46:40,548 --> 00:46:42,049
I feel so bad for them.

671
00:46:43,050 --> 00:46:44,885
But as far as I know,

672
00:46:44,969 --> 00:46:48,806
she got along fine with her friends.

673
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:51,434
Well, that's what I heard...

674
00:46:52,268 --> 00:46:54,228
[Jaehong] You know this student too?

675
00:46:55,187 --> 00:46:59,150
I don't know her that well.
We just say hi when passing by on campus.

676
00:46:59,358 --> 00:47:00,901
You say hi when you pass each other?

677
00:47:00,985 --> 00:47:03,070
-You don't know her well?
-[Minjae] Right.

678
00:47:04,322 --> 00:47:09,702
Do you know the saying,
<i>"Biinbujeon Bujaeseungdeok"?</i>

679
00:47:09,785 --> 00:47:11,287
Yes, I do.

680
00:47:12,663 --> 00:47:15,833
People of poor character
should hold no position of authority.

681
00:47:15,916 --> 00:47:17,918
Nor should they be taught valuable skills.

682
00:47:18,419 --> 00:47:21,922
And that talent and knowledge
should never take precedence over virtue.

683
00:47:22,006 --> 00:47:24,717
[Jaehong] There's a saying like that?
That's a great one.

684
00:47:25,301 --> 00:47:28,721
[Miran laughs] There is.
God, you engineers are so uncultured.

685
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:30,014
I know, right?

686
00:47:30,598 --> 00:47:31,766
Except for you, Mr. Park.

687
00:47:34,477 --> 00:47:35,478
Yeah.

688
00:47:36,228 --> 00:47:38,939
[Miran] Now that you're pursuing
an academic career

689
00:47:39,023 --> 00:47:41,525
and will be teaching students yourself,

690
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,445
I hope you'll keep that in mind.

691
00:47:45,529 --> 00:47:46,530
I will.

692
00:47:47,615 --> 00:47:49,408
Well, I should keep it in mind.

693
00:47:49,492 --> 00:47:52,411
But who said that? Was it Confucius?

694
00:47:53,704 --> 00:47:55,456
You don't need to know.

695
00:47:55,539 --> 00:47:57,583
Even if I told you,
you'd forget it anyway.

696
00:47:57,666 --> 00:47:59,668
Yeah, a hundred percent.

697
00:48:08,427 --> 00:48:09,428
-Subin.
-[Subin] Yes.

698
00:48:09,512 --> 00:48:11,430
-Can I have a cup of green tea?
-Sure.

699
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:26,028
-[Subin] Here's your tea.
-Yeah. Thanks.

700
00:48:29,532 --> 00:48:31,909
Have you been in touch with Youjin lately?

701
00:48:31,992 --> 00:48:32,993
Ah...

702
00:48:33,536 --> 00:48:35,413
No, I haven't.

703
00:48:36,122 --> 00:48:37,123
Yeah?

704
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:40,876
She contacted the mechanical engineering
department. Did you know?

705
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,169
Mechanical engineering?

706
00:48:43,295 --> 00:48:44,296
Uh...

707
00:48:44,380 --> 00:48:46,507
Hmm. So you didn't know.

708
00:48:47,842 --> 00:48:51,679
You two were so close as undergrads.
And you don't even keep in touch now?

709
00:48:52,888 --> 00:48:55,433
-We're both really busy, so...
-[Miran] Yeah.

710
00:48:56,016 --> 00:48:57,518
You're both busy.

711
00:48:57,601 --> 00:48:59,687
Friends are only friends
when they stay close.

712
00:48:59,770 --> 00:49:01,480
Once you drift apart, it's pointless.

713
00:49:02,565 --> 00:49:03,566
See?

714
00:49:03,649 --> 00:49:08,154
I'm telling you, I'm the only one
who looks out for you, Subin.

715
00:49:26,547 --> 00:49:27,548
Hello.

716
00:49:29,049 --> 00:49:30,468
What brings you here?

717
00:49:31,552 --> 00:49:32,553
Uh...

718
00:49:33,179 --> 00:49:36,807
I heard he ended up in the hospital
after Youjin hit him.

719
00:49:37,641 --> 00:49:39,852
Ah, he was hospitalized?

720
00:49:42,813 --> 00:49:46,150
He said he'd sue us if we sued him.

721
00:49:47,234 --> 00:49:49,862
I was so scared
and didn't know what to do.

722
00:49:50,821 --> 00:49:53,324
So I told Professor Kang about it,
and she helped me.

723
00:49:53,407 --> 00:49:55,075
She even paid the hospital bills.

724
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,286
So you two were...

725
00:49:59,288 --> 00:50:01,665
not dating or anything...

726
00:50:01,749 --> 00:50:03,250
[Sujin] No, absolutely not.

727
00:50:04,919 --> 00:50:08,005
The professor said
we could just go with that and move on

728
00:50:08,923 --> 00:50:11,926
since we wouldn't have
to see each other again anyway

729
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:14,845
and there was no need
to make a bigger deal out of it.

730
00:50:16,013 --> 00:50:17,848
So that's what we did.

731
00:50:18,724 --> 00:50:19,725
Oh.

732
00:50:20,726 --> 00:50:21,810
Honestly,

733
00:50:22,645 --> 00:50:26,148
being questioned at the police station
wasn't exactly pleasant.

734
00:50:26,232 --> 00:50:27,608
It was really scary.

735
00:50:27,691 --> 00:50:28,776
But...

736
00:50:29,735 --> 00:50:32,655
Lim Youjin didn't seem to know about that.

737
00:50:35,491 --> 00:50:38,494
And you two stopped talking to each other.

738
00:50:41,497 --> 00:50:42,915
Would that also happen to be

739
00:50:42,998 --> 00:50:45,709
because of something
Professor Kang Miran said?

740
00:50:49,004 --> 00:50:51,090
What is it? What did she say?

741
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:55,970
Youjin wouldn't listen to the professor.

742
00:50:56,887 --> 00:51:01,642
And that wasn't all.
I heard she even talked back to her.

743
00:51:02,977 --> 00:51:03,978
Hmm.

744
00:51:05,104 --> 00:51:08,524
Now, no one in our department
can talk to Youjin anymore.

745
00:51:12,611 --> 00:51:14,280
GRADUATE SCHOOL APPLICATION FORM

746
00:51:14,363 --> 00:51:16,991
LIM YOUJIN
AHN JAEHONG

747
00:51:22,663 --> 00:51:24,957
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
GRADUATE SCHOOL APPLICATION

748
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:26,417
MECHANICAL ENGINEERING

749
00:51:33,382 --> 00:51:35,342
YOUR APPLICATION
HAS BEEN SUCCESSFULLY SUBMITTED

750
00:52:49,875 --> 00:52:50,918
Oh.

751
00:52:52,002 --> 00:52:53,003
Hi.

752
00:53:08,769 --> 00:53:09,770
[Sejin] Hello.

753
00:53:09,853 --> 00:53:12,564
Hi. You can sit wherever you want.

754
00:53:35,337 --> 00:53:37,131
-Here.
-Thank you.

755
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:54,440
DERIVE THE ROTATION MATRIX
FOR ZYX EULER ANGLES

756
00:53:55,733 --> 00:53:57,234
Have any of you seen <i>Good Will Hunting?</i>

757
00:53:58,527 --> 00:53:59,528
I have.

758
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:01,321
I haven't.

759
00:54:01,905 --> 00:54:05,617
It's a movie.
The main character's a math genius.

760
00:54:05,701 --> 00:54:07,703
If you haven't seen it,
make sure you do sometime.

761
00:54:07,786 --> 00:54:09,204
It's a classic.

762
00:54:09,872 --> 00:54:11,707
And what if you haven't watched it?

763
00:54:11,790 --> 00:54:14,168
It has nothing to do with this. It's okay.

764
00:54:37,691 --> 00:54:38,734
[Youjin] Excuse me.

765
00:54:39,777 --> 00:54:40,778
What is it?

766
00:54:44,406 --> 00:54:45,616
You don't know Euler angles?

767
00:54:46,200 --> 00:54:49,703
I mean... Do we have to use Euler angles?

768
00:54:49,786 --> 00:54:51,163
Oh.

769
00:54:51,788 --> 00:54:55,459
Isn't that obvious? You need to solve it
the way the question asks.

770
00:54:56,043 --> 00:54:57,753
Just do what you can.

771
00:55:00,589 --> 00:55:02,341
All right. You may begin.

772
00:56:31,013 --> 00:56:33,015
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER

773
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:13,722
Was it a little too difficult?

774
00:57:13,805 --> 00:57:14,806
Ah.

775
00:57:15,432 --> 00:57:19,353
Well, I just blanked
on the harmonic addition theorem.

776
00:57:19,436 --> 00:57:20,562
Hmm.

777
00:57:28,028 --> 00:57:29,071
Good work.

778
00:57:34,368 --> 00:57:37,037
I'm really sorry
about what happened that day.

779
00:57:38,205 --> 00:57:39,331
Hmm?

780
00:57:39,414 --> 00:57:41,500
I know I've got some nerve

781
00:57:41,583 --> 00:57:44,670
asking you to let me back into the lab
after the huge mess I caused.

782
00:57:45,629 --> 00:57:47,255
But please give me one more chance.

783
00:57:48,674 --> 00:57:52,678
Seeing the robot in person
made me love robotics even more.

784
00:57:53,345 --> 00:57:54,638
I really want to study it.

785
00:57:54,721 --> 00:57:55,722
Hmm.

786
00:57:56,682 --> 00:57:57,683
Okay.

787
00:57:59,643 --> 00:58:00,852
Good work today.

788
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:05,148
You said it'd be a waste of four years.

789
00:58:06,817 --> 00:58:09,236
But why is that a waste?
It was a learning experience.

790
00:58:11,363 --> 00:58:13,782
Everyone stumbles and fails sometimes,

791
00:58:14,825 --> 00:58:19,329
but I believe we have to learn from it,
pick ourselves back up, and keep going.

792
00:58:23,041 --> 00:58:24,793
I'm sorry if that was out of line.

793
00:58:28,296 --> 00:58:29,297
But...

794
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:33,927
what are you going to do
if you fail the test?

795
00:58:34,428 --> 00:58:35,762
Then...

796
00:58:37,347 --> 00:58:40,267
I'll take another one until I get in.

797
00:58:41,935 --> 00:58:42,936
You can go now.

798
00:58:43,812 --> 00:58:44,813
Okay.

799
00:58:59,369 --> 00:59:02,873
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
LIM YOUJIN

800
00:59:02,956 --> 00:59:07,043
She basically wrote a whole thesis here.

801
00:59:10,464 --> 00:59:12,591
One is a nutjob,

802
00:59:12,674 --> 00:59:16,595
and the other one's got
some personality issues.

803
00:59:16,678 --> 00:59:18,263
-[Minjae] Oh...
-A nutjob would be better, right?

804
00:59:18,764 --> 00:59:22,350
I mean, our research
involves a lot of teamwork.

805
00:59:26,021 --> 00:59:27,731
Well,

806
00:59:27,814 --> 00:59:31,401
she can be pretty stubborn
and a little eccentric,

807
00:59:31,985 --> 00:59:36,198
but she definitely doesn't have
any serious character issues.

808
00:59:38,074 --> 00:59:41,703
And from what I've seen,
she seems very determined to study.

809
00:59:43,246 --> 00:59:47,501
Unless there are any major concerns
about her abilities,

810
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:52,172
I personally think
we'd be fine admitting her...

811
00:59:55,008 --> 00:59:57,344
She wrote so tiny
I can barely even read it.

812
00:59:58,136 --> 01:00:02,349
Or maybe we should
just show this to Professor Lee.

813
01:00:02,432 --> 01:00:03,642
That could work.

814
01:00:05,101 --> 01:00:07,103
I wonder
if Professor Lee is in his office.

815
01:00:08,897 --> 01:00:11,608
[Jaehong] How was your first semester
teaching Korean students

816
01:00:11,691 --> 01:00:13,568
after teaching in the US?

817
01:00:13,652 --> 01:00:15,821
Well, we have
a very different talent pool here.

818
01:00:15,904 --> 01:00:17,906
Yeah, that's true,

819
01:00:17,989 --> 01:00:19,825
but we have
plenty of talented students too.

820
01:00:19,908 --> 01:00:20,909
Right.

821
01:00:20,992 --> 01:00:23,119
[Jaehong] It all depends
on the teacher, though.

822
01:00:24,788 --> 01:00:27,290
Still, it's good
to be back in Korea, right?

823
01:00:28,041 --> 01:00:31,253
I mean, the food is great here.

824
01:00:33,338 --> 01:00:34,422
Yeah, that's true.

825
01:00:38,468 --> 01:00:40,053
-Is this a female student?
-Hmm?

826
01:00:40,929 --> 01:00:41,930
Yes.

827
01:00:42,013 --> 01:00:43,014
Hmm...

828
01:00:44,808 --> 01:00:46,893
-It's good.
-It's good?

829
01:00:46,977 --> 01:00:48,520
I can tell she's got talent.

830
01:00:49,062 --> 01:00:51,273
But why does she want to study
mechanical engineering?

831
01:00:51,356 --> 01:00:54,776
Well, because machines are more fun
than math, obviously.

832
01:00:55,277 --> 01:00:58,071
Ah, she can join the math program.
We'll take her.

833
01:00:58,154 --> 01:01:00,615
We can't do that.
We need more students too.

834
01:01:00,699 --> 01:01:02,784
-Yes.
-Right? It's serious.

835
01:01:02,868 --> 01:01:06,538
Well, she said she wanted to study
mechanical engineering, so...

836
01:01:06,621 --> 01:01:10,917
Exactly. We should respect
what she wants to do.

837
01:01:11,001 --> 01:01:13,420
Tell her to contact our department,
just in case.

838
01:01:13,503 --> 01:01:16,298
Come on, I said we can't.
Stop trying to steal our student.

839
01:01:16,381 --> 01:01:18,383
-Just in case.
-No way.

840
01:01:19,968 --> 01:01:21,136
Don't even think about it.

841
01:01:22,971 --> 01:01:24,598
He's really hard to impress.

842
01:01:24,681 --> 01:01:26,308
If even he's saying that,

843
01:01:27,183 --> 01:01:28,935
she must be a real genius.

844
01:01:29,019 --> 01:01:30,228
-Watch out.
-It's okay.

845
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:34,357
I don't know if she's a genius...

846
01:01:34,441 --> 01:01:36,026
-You know, Minjae.
-Yes.

847
01:01:36,109 --> 01:01:38,445
You really do have a good eye for people.

848
01:01:38,528 --> 01:01:39,529
Not at all.

849
01:01:41,197 --> 01:01:44,701
I guess this could be a good chance
for us to prepare for the WRS.

850
01:01:45,952 --> 01:01:48,788
I heard they're already
preparing for it at KAIST.

851
01:01:48,872 --> 01:01:52,083
Really? If they can do it,
there's no way we can't.

852
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:54,169
-Right.
-Oh, man.

853
01:01:54,252 --> 01:01:58,298
My heart's racing just thinking
about crushing them this time.

854
01:02:01,134 --> 01:02:04,971
So, what are we going to do
with Lim Youjin?

855
01:02:05,055 --> 01:02:06,348
Are we admitting her?

856
01:02:07,140 --> 01:02:09,351
Why would a genius
get rejected from grad school?

857
01:02:09,434 --> 01:02:11,311
What are you even talking about?

858
01:02:13,772 --> 01:02:15,190
-[Youseong] Mmm. [slurps]
-[Youjin screams]

859
01:02:15,273 --> 01:02:16,942
-[Youseong] This is good.
-[door opens]

860
01:02:17,025 --> 01:02:18,360
-What's going on?
-[footsteps approaching]

861
01:02:18,443 --> 01:02:19,444
-What is it?
-[Youjin] Mom!

862
01:02:19,527 --> 01:02:20,654
[Youseong] It's seasoned perfectly.

863
01:02:20,737 --> 01:02:21,905
-[Youjin] I got in.
-What?

864
01:02:21,988 --> 01:02:24,032
I got it. I got in!

865
01:02:24,115 --> 01:02:26,785
-Oh, my God! Well done, Youjin!
-I got into grad school!

866
01:02:26,868 --> 01:02:29,120
[Miyoung] Well done!

867
01:02:29,204 --> 01:02:31,623
My girl, well done!

868
01:02:32,123 --> 01:02:34,542
If she studied that much
and still didn't get in,

869
01:02:34,626 --> 01:02:36,628
she'd be worse than an idiot.

870
01:02:38,922 --> 01:02:42,717
You did a great job.
That's my girl. Well done!

871
01:03:17,419 --> 01:03:18,753
-[Hangyeol] She's here.
-[Taeho] Hmm?

872
01:03:18,837 --> 01:03:20,338
-I'm sorry I'm late.
-[Taeho] Hey!

873
01:03:20,422 --> 01:03:22,674
No, you're not late.

874
01:03:22,757 --> 01:03:25,760
Let's see. See? You came right on time.

875
01:03:25,844 --> 01:03:28,221
As your junior,
I should've come earlier and waited.

876
01:03:28,304 --> 01:03:31,725
Well, I appreciate
your respect for seniority.

877
01:03:32,892 --> 01:03:34,519
You can drop the formalities with me.

878
01:03:36,354 --> 01:03:37,731
Can I really do that?

879
01:03:40,775 --> 01:03:44,779
[hesitates] Okay, then. Youjin.

880
01:03:47,449 --> 01:03:49,617
-Does that go for me too?
-Sure.

881
01:03:49,701 --> 01:03:52,746
-Then I guess I'll do the same.
-Of course.

882
01:03:54,039 --> 01:03:56,458
You're really easygoing.

883
01:03:57,417 --> 01:03:58,960
When is Minjae going to join us?

884
01:03:59,044 --> 01:04:02,213
-Hold on.
-Minjae is coming with Chacha.

885
01:04:02,297 --> 01:04:03,798
-[Taeho] Yeah.
-Chacha?

886
01:04:06,217 --> 01:04:10,889
I'm sure you've met her once.
You know, at the GN Electronics office.

887
01:04:11,473 --> 01:04:13,141
Ah, Ms. Cha?

888
01:04:13,224 --> 01:04:15,435
She used to be in our lab.

889
01:04:16,102 --> 01:04:17,103
Yeah, I know.

890
01:04:17,187 --> 01:04:20,106
They're just around the corner.
Should we go ahead and order?

891
01:04:23,109 --> 01:04:24,110
[Hangyeol] There they come.

892
01:04:24,736 --> 01:04:25,820
-[Taeho] Huh? Yeah.
-[Hangyeol] Hey.

893
01:04:27,489 --> 01:04:29,199
[Seohyun] Traffic is awful around here.

894
01:04:31,117 --> 01:04:32,285
[Seohyun] Oh.

895
01:04:32,368 --> 01:04:33,620
Hello.

896
01:04:34,662 --> 01:04:37,999
-[Minjae] Why haven't you ordered yet?
-Well... What should we order?

897
01:04:38,750 --> 01:04:40,376
[Minjae] Oh, no. Hey.

898
01:04:41,044 --> 01:04:42,462
-[Taeho] All right.
-[bottle clinking]

899
01:04:44,214 --> 01:04:49,177
Let's welcome our newest lab member,
Lim Youjin.

900
01:04:49,260 --> 01:04:50,762
Give her a hand!

901
01:04:54,432 --> 01:04:55,767
Now,

902
01:04:55,850 --> 01:04:59,896
let's hear a few words from Youjin.

903
01:05:05,735 --> 01:05:09,989
Hmm, I... I mean,
although I'm from a different major,

904
01:05:10,073 --> 01:05:13,618
uh, and I don't know a lot
about robotics research,

905
01:05:14,494 --> 01:05:19,332
I'll work hard and make sure
I pull my weight as part of the team.

906
01:05:23,670 --> 01:05:25,380
Wait a minute.

907
01:05:25,880 --> 01:05:28,133
You can't sit down just yet.

908
01:05:29,801 --> 01:05:32,428
Please sing a song.

909
01:05:32,929 --> 01:05:34,389
I can't sing. No, I can't sing.

910
01:05:34,472 --> 01:05:38,059
[chanting] Sing! Sing!

911
01:05:38,143 --> 01:05:42,355
-Sing! Sing!
-Sing! Sing!

912
01:06:39,746 --> 01:06:41,873
You guys are in trouble now.

913
01:06:41,956 --> 01:06:44,417
Your newbie is quite a character.

914
01:06:48,171 --> 01:06:49,297
-[customer gasps]
-[Seohyun gasps]

915
01:06:49,380 --> 01:06:50,757
[Hangyeol] Hey, Youjin.

916
01:06:50,840 --> 01:06:51,841
Youjin!

917
01:06:52,342 --> 01:06:53,343
Excuse me!

918
01:06:59,974 --> 01:07:03,645
<i>Please send us your messages</i>

919
01:07:03,728 --> 01:07:06,814
<i>online or by text at 93001.</i>

920
01:07:18,326 --> 01:07:20,370
-[Youjin] Hmm...
-[softly] Her snore...

921
01:07:42,350 --> 01:07:43,351
Thank you.

922
01:08:02,662 --> 01:08:05,748
So, where do you live?

923
01:08:05,832 --> 01:08:07,625
I'll take you home.

924
01:08:07,709 --> 01:08:08,710
Mmm.

925
01:08:08,793 --> 01:08:11,004
No, it's okay. I can go home by myself.

926
01:08:11,963 --> 01:08:13,381
You're not going home alone.

927
01:08:14,632 --> 01:08:16,217
Come on, where do you live?

928
01:08:16,301 --> 01:08:19,387
No, really. I'm completely sober now.

929
01:08:20,555 --> 01:08:22,390
-Good night, then.
-But...

930
01:08:25,601 --> 01:08:27,020
Be careful.

931
01:08:29,063 --> 01:08:30,064
Oh, my God.

932
01:08:31,566 --> 01:08:32,567
Your bag.

933
01:08:33,276 --> 01:08:35,111
You forgot your bag. [groans]

934
01:08:37,322 --> 01:08:38,698
Take your hand out. Like this.

935
01:08:38,781 --> 01:08:40,199
-Huh?
-Your bag.

936
01:08:42,285 --> 01:08:44,162
[Youjin] Thank you. Bye.

937
01:08:48,166 --> 01:08:49,417
-[thuds]
-Ah.

938
01:08:52,587 --> 01:08:56,257
Okay, fine. Come here. Come this way.

939
01:09:02,263 --> 01:09:03,264
Here.

940
01:09:04,015 --> 01:09:06,934
Sit here and sober up a little
before you head home.

941
01:09:09,187 --> 01:09:12,273
Actually, wait. Just stay right here.

942
01:09:26,329 --> 01:09:27,330
I'll just have this.

943
01:09:27,413 --> 01:09:29,207
-[staff] All right.
-[scanner beeps]

944
01:09:29,791 --> 01:09:31,918
-Okay, insert your card.
-Okay.

945
01:09:35,463 --> 01:09:37,256
-[staff] You're all set.
-Thank you.

946
01:10:26,889 --> 01:10:28,891
-[pants]
-[meowing]

947
01:10:39,652 --> 01:10:40,653
Oh, boy.

948
01:10:41,821 --> 01:10:44,907
What are you doing here?

949
01:10:45,950 --> 01:10:48,286
It's cold out here.
Why did you leave your bag?

950
01:10:50,288 --> 01:10:51,289
Drink this.

951
01:10:59,046 --> 01:11:00,715
If you don't want this, tell me now.

952
01:11:03,468 --> 01:11:04,469
Five.

953
01:11:05,595 --> 01:11:06,596
Four.

954
01:11:08,222 --> 01:11:09,223
Three.

955
01:11:10,683 --> 01:11:11,684
Two.

956
01:11:13,686 --> 01:11:14,687
One.

957
01:12:02,985 --> 01:12:06,906
BETWEEN STEPS

958
01:12:06,989 --> 01:12:07,990
Hi.

959
01:12:08,074 --> 01:12:11,077
It's not like
I have a lot of dating experience,

960
01:12:11,160 --> 01:12:12,537
so I'm not sure.

961
01:12:12,620 --> 01:12:14,455
<i>I was pretty drunk that day too.</i>

962
01:12:14,539 --> 01:12:17,625
-[Sejin] Are those two a couple?
-[Taeho] High school sweethearts.

963
01:12:17,708 --> 01:12:19,752
-Please, just one picture with this.
-No.

964
01:12:19,836 --> 01:12:21,838
When did I disrespect you?

965
01:12:21,921 --> 01:12:24,549
[Subin] <i>The lab assistant</i>
<i>is that guy from earlier, right?</i>

966
01:12:24,632 --> 01:12:27,385
[Minjae] <i>Do you want some ice cream?</i>
<i>What flavor do you like?</i>

967
01:12:27,468 --> 01:12:28,928
She's not even that pretty.

968
01:12:29,011 --> 01:12:30,596
[Youjin] <i>A goddess. A genius goddess.</i>

969
01:12:30,680 --> 01:12:32,807
[laughing] You're really cute.
